Daniil TV: retain a v2 piece until its pending hash callback completes.

Root-only metadata and cache turnover can let another piece's block hashes
validate a finished adjacent piece whose own hash job is still outstanding.
piece_flushed() removes that piece's download state and requires hashing == 0;
its pending callback must instead finish verification and accounting itself.
Keep the piece pending without weakening any hash check or picker assertion.

Regression: eviction_v2_adjacent_hash_completion_keeps_pending_callback_alive
stages that exact callback order with generated bytes and real Merkle hashes.
The unpatched source aborts at piece_picker::piece_flushed (hashing == 0).

diff --git a/src/torrent.cpp b/src/torrent.cpp
--- a/src/torrent.cpp
+++ b/src/torrent.cpp
@@ -4843,7 +4843,10 @@ namespace {
 		{
 			for (piece_index_t verified_piece : adjacent_verified)
 			{
-				if (m_picker->have_piece(verified_piece)) continue;
+				// A pending hash callback still owns this piece's download state.
+				// Let that callback finish it, even if these hashes validate it too.
+				if (m_picker->have_piece(verified_piece)
+					|| m_picker->is_hashing(verified_piece)) continue;
 				// we_have() has not been called yet for this piece — confirm the bit is clear
 #if TORRENT_USE_INVARIANT_CHECKS
 				TORRENT_ASSERT(!m_file_progress.have_piece(verified_piece));
